# NestJS Development Standards

## Path Aliases

```typescript
// ✅ Use aliases
import { ResponseHelper } from '@core/shared/helpers/response.helper';
import { ApiException } from '@core/shared/exceptions/api.exception';

// ❌ Avoid relative imports
import { ResponseHelper } from '../../../core/shared/helpers/response.helper';
```

## Exception Handling

Services use `ApiException`, not NestJS exceptions:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
const message = i18n.t('users.notFound');
throw ApiException.notFound(message);

// ❌ Wrong
throw new NotFoundException('User not found');
```

## Controller Pattern

No try-catch, use ResponseHelper with i18n:

```typescript
async create(
  @Body() dto: CreateDto,
  @AuditRequestInfo() auditInfo: AuditInfo,
  @I18n() i18n: I18nContext<I18nTranslations>,
  @Res() response: Response
) {
  const result = await this.service.create(dto, auditInfo, i18n);
  const message = i18n.t('users.created');
  ResponseHelper.created(result, response, message);
}
```

## Service Pattern

Pass i18n context, use Prisma, use audit helper:

```typescript
async create(
  dto: CreateDto,
  auditInfo: AuditInfo,
  i18n: I18nContext<I18nTranslations>
): Promise<UserResponse> {
  const auditFields = createAuditFields(auditInfo);
  // ... business logic
}
```

## Response Classes

Extend BaseResponseTransformer:

```typescript
export class ItemResponse extends BaseResponseTransformer {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}
// Usage: ItemResponse.from(data), ItemResponse.fromMany(data)
```

## Quick Rules

- Use `??` not `||` for nullish coalescing
- Always add explicit return types
- Use `createAuditFields(auditInfo)` for audit fields
- Use Prisma `$transaction` for related operations
- Translate first, then pass message to ResponseHelper/ApiException
